          "transliteration": "qul",
          "isIsmFail": false,
          "isHarf": false,
          "wordType": "Fi'l",
          "root": "ق و ل",
          "meaning": "Say",
          "explanation": "Imperative verb (fi'l amr), second person masculine singular. It is built upon sukun (mabni 'ala al-sukun). The underlying form is 'uqlul' with the weak letter (waw) dropped to avoid two sukun meeting."
        },
        {
          "word": "أَعُوذُ",
          "transliteration": "a'ūdhu",
          "isIsmFail": false,
          "isHarf": false,
          "wordType": "Fi'l",
          "root": "ع و ذ",
          "meaning": "I seek refuge",
          "explanation": "Present tense verb (fi'l mudari'), first person singular, imperfect. It is marfu' (nominative) due to the absence of any nasib or jazim particles, with the sign of raf' being the damma."
        },
        {
          "word": "بِرَبِّ",
          "transliteration": "birabbi",
          "isIsmFail": false,
          "isHarf": true,
          "wordType": "Harf",
          "root": "ر ب ب",
          "meaning": "in the Lord",
          "explanation": "Ba is a preposition (harf jar) denoting connection/seeking help (isti'anah). Rabb is a noun (ism majrur) governed by the ba, with the kasra as the sign of jarr."
        },
        {
          "word": "ٱلنَّاسِ",
          "transliteration": "an-nāsi",
          "isIsmFail": false,
          "isHarf": false,
          "wordType": "Ism",
          "root": "ن و س",
          "meaning": "of mankind",
          "explanation": "Definite noun (ism mu'arraf bi-al-lam), genitive (majrur) as it is a mudaf ilayh (possessive complement) to Rabb."
        }
      ]
    },
